                                                        <script>
                                                            const faqData = {
                                                                general: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What are game QA services?",
                                                                        a: "Game QA services are the structured process of testing a game's functionality, stability, performance, and platform compliance against documented requirements by producing actionable defect reports that development teams use to fix issues before they reach players or platform holders."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is the difference between game QA and playtesting?",
                                                                        a: "Playtesting evaluates a game's fun, feel, and design from a player perspective with subjective feedback on experience. Game QA testing services are methodical, documentation-based testing against defined requirements."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "When in production should game QA testing begin?",
                                                                        a: "QA integration should begin from early sprint cycles, as soon as the first features are testable. Defects found in the sprint they're introduced cost significantly less to fix than defects found at the end of production; the schedule is compressed, and every fix carries regression risk."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is video game quality assurance outsourcing?",
                                                                        a: "Video game quality assurance outsourcing is contracting an external game testing company to run QA functions with functional testing, regression, platform compliance, localization, and specialized testing disciplines rather than maintaining a full internal QA department."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Does Clarisco provide QA services for indie game studios?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our QA services for indie game studios are specifically structured for small teams with transparent per-sprint pricing, test plans built against whatever documentation exists rather than requiring full GDD completion, and a QA lead who functions as the studio's complete QA function."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What platforms does Clarisco's game testing company cover?",
                                                                        a: "Our game QA testing services cover PlayStation 5, Xbox Series X|S, Nintendo Switch, iOS, Android, PC (Steam and Epic Games Store), WebGL, and Meta Quest VR with platform-specific compliance testing experience across TRC, TCR, LotCheck, App Store, and Google Play requirements."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How does game QA outsourcing integrate with an internal development team?",
                                                                        a: "Our QA teams are integrated into your bug tracking system, build delivery pipeline, and the sprint reporting cadence by operating as a functional extension of your team rather than an external vendor receiving periodic build drops for isolated testing sessions."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is a test plan and why does it matter for game QA?",
                                                                        a: "A test plan is a documented specification of what will be tested, how it will be tested, and what a passing result looks like per feature and platform requirement. Test plans ensure QA coverage is complete and verifiable rather than dependent on a tester's judgment about what to check."
                                                                    }
                                                                ],
                                                                business: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What does functional QA testing for games cover?",
                                                                        a: "Functional QA testing for games validates every feature, system interaction, UI flow, and edge case against the design specification by producing defect reports with full reproduction evidence for every failure. Coverage includes positive paths, negative paths, boundary conditions, and unexpected user behavior sequences that informal testing routinely misses."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Does Clarisco handle platform certification testing?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our console game testing services cover PlayStation TRC, Xbox TCR, and Nintendo Switch LotCheck compliance testing with systematic tests against current platform requirements, with compliance self-assessment documentation produced before submission build preparation begins."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What does localization QA testing include?",
                                                                        a: "Our localization QA testing covers text truncation, font rendering, missing string identification, encoding errors, subtitle timing accuracy, dubbed audio sync, audio level consistency, cultural appropriateness review, and UI layout integrity."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Do you offer multiplayer and network testing?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our multiplayer game testing covers session creation, matchmaking, state synchronization under simulated latency conditions, disconnection and reconnection handling, host migration, server load under concurrent player counts, anti-cheat validation, and cross-platform play parity testing."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What does mobile game QA testing include?",
                                                                        a: "Our mobile game QA testing covers device compatibility across iOS and Android hardware matrices, OS version compatibility, touch input validation, monetization SDK testing, crash reproduction, push notification behaviour, App Store and Google Play pre-submission compliance, and binary submission support."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Does Clarisco build automated test suites for game projects?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our automated game testing services include custom test suite development using Unity Test Framework, Unreal Automation System, or platform-native frameworks with scripted regression agents, crash detection automation, frame rate benchmarking, and CI/CD pipeline integration for daily build testing."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is accessibility testing for games?",
                                                                        a: "Accessibility testing validates a game against platform accessibility guidelines with subtitle size and background opacity, remappable controls, colorblind mode effectiveness, text size options, audio cue visual alternatives, and navigation without audio.  "
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Can Clarisco test iGaming and real-money game platforms?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our QA practice for regulated real-money games covers transaction flow testing across all payment methods and price tiers, RNG output statistical validation, economy accuracy testing, regulatory compliance testing, cross-device compatibility, and age verification flow testing."
                                                                    }
                                                                ],

                                                                pricing: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How much do game QA services cost?",
                                                                        a: "Game QA cost depends on scope, platform count, team size, and testing disciplines required. Sprint-integrated QA for a mobile title typically starts from $3,000–$8,000 per sprint for a small team. Console certification testing packages typically range from $8,000–$25,000+ depending on platform count and compliance scope."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How long does a game QA engagement take to deliver first results?",
                                                                        a: "First defect reports are typically delivered within five to seven business days of test plan sign-off by covering the test environment setup, build access configuration, and initial functional testing pass. For end-of-production QA sprints, the full testing engagement is time-boxed to your submission window with coverage."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How does Clarisco integrate into our existing bug tracking system?",
                                                                        a: "Our QA teams work directly inside your Jira, TestRail, Hansoft, or Notion setup by filing defects to your agreed template, using your severity classifications and component labels, and following your sprint workflow for defect review and close verification. "
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is included in a platform certification QA package?",
                                                                        a: "A certification QA package includes systematic compliance testing against current TRC/TCR/LotCheck or App Store/Google Play requirements, a compliance test report with citation and severity per finding, a compliance self-assessment document, submission build verification, and certification response management."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How does Clarisco price QA engagements?",
                                                                        a: "QA engagements are priced as a sprint retainer, a fixed-scope package, or time-and-materials. The right model depends on your production stage and testing discipline requirements."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Can Clarisco handle QA for a game that has already launched and needs ongoing testing?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our post-launch QA retainer maintains the regression baseline from the launch build and applies it to every content update, seasonal event, balance patch, and platform OS compatibility change by delivering test reports before each release rather than after player-reported defects surface in store reviews."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Who owns the test plans, test suites, and defect data produced during a QA engagement?",
                                                                        a: "All test plans, test case libraries, automated test scripts, and defect data produced during a Clarisco QA engagement are delivered to the client at engagement completion by providing a documented QA foundation that an internal team or future QA vendor can continue from without starting over."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How do I evaluate whether my game is ready for platform certification?",
                                                                        a: "Our pre-certification readiness assessment reviews your current build against TRC/TCR/LotCheck requirements, documents open compliance risks, and produces a prioritized remediation list before you commit to a submission timeline by giving you an accurate picture of certification readiness."
                                                                    }
                                                                ]
                                                            };

                                                            function createFaq(section, id) {
                                                                const container = document.getElementById(id);
                                                                faqData[section].forEach((item, index) => {
                                                                    const html = `<div class="accordion-item">
                                                                        <p class="accordion-header">
                                                                        <button class="accordion-button ${index !== 0 ? 'collapsed' : ''}" 
                                                                        data-bs-toggle="collapse" 
                                                                        data-bs-target="#${section}${index}">
                                                                        <span class="faq-icon"><i class="bi bi-book"></i></span>
                                                                        <span class="faq-title">${item.q}</span>
                                                                        </button>
                                                                        </p>
                                                                        <div id="${section}${index}" class="accordion-collapse collapse ${index === 0 ? 'show' : ''}"  data-bs-parent="#${id}">
                                                                        <div class="accordion-body">${item.a}</div>
                                                                        </div>
                                                                        </div>`;
                                                                    container.insertAdjacentHTML("beforeend", html);
                                                                });
                                                            }
                                                            createFaq("general", "generalFaq");
                                                            createFaq("business", "businessFaq");
                                                            createFaq("pricing", "pricingFaq");
                                                        </script>

                                                        <script>
                                                            $(document).ready(function ($) {
                                                                //Check if an element was in a screen
                                                                function isScrolledIntoView(elem) {
                                                                    var docViewTop = $(window).scrollTop();
                                                                    var docViewBottom = docViewTop + $(window).height();
                                                                    var elemTop = $(elem).offset().top;
                                                                    var elemBottom = elemTop + $(elem).height();
                                                                    return ((elemBottom <= docViewBottom));
                                                                }
                                                                //Count up code
                                                                function countUp() {
                                                                    $('.counter').each(function () {
                                                                        var $this = $(this), // <- Don't touch this variable. It's pure magic.
                                                                            countTo = $this.attr('data-count');
                                                                        ended = $this.attr('ended');

                                                                        if (ended != "true" && isScrolledIntoView($this)) {
                                                                            $({ countNum: $this.text() }).animate({
                                                                                countNum: countTo
                                                                            },
                                                                                {
                                                                                    duration: 2500, //duration of counting
                                                                                    easing: 'swing',
                                                                                    step: function () {
                                                                                        $this.text(Math.floor(this.countNum));
                                                                                    },
                                                                                    complete: function () {
                                                                                        $this.text(this.countNum);
                                                                                    }
